  "generated_text": "First, we start with the given quadratic equation:\n\\[ x^2 - 3x + 9 = x + 41 \\]\n\nNext, we move all terms to one side of the equation to set it to zero:\n\n x x^ - - 3x +  - - x - 41 = 0 \\]\n\\[ x^2 - 4x -  2 = 0 \\]\n\n\n\nNow, we factor the quadratic equation:\n\\[ (x - 4)(x +  ) = 0 \\]\n\n\n\n us factor the quadratic equation:\n\\[ (x - 4)(x + 8) = 0 \\]\n\n\n\n\n solutions the solutions solutions\n\\[ x - 4 = 0 \\implies x = 4 \\]\n\\[ x + 8 = 0 \\implies x = -8 \\]\n\n\n\nThe positive difference between these solutions is:\n\\[ |4 - (-8)| = |4 + 8| = |12| = 12 \\]\n\n\n\nTherefore, the positive difference between the solutions is:\n\\[\\boxed{12} \\]",
